WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:03.500
A city name is not a boarding station.

2
00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:10.000
NDLS and NZM are different railway stations.

3
00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:18.500
If one train arrives at one and the next leaves from the other, allow for the station exit, road journey and boarding time.

4
00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:22.000
Match the exact codes on both tickets.

5
00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:27.000
A timetable connection alone does not tell you whether that transfer will work for your group.

6
00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:33.000
Before booking a connection, compare station codes—not just city names.

